                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>24.10.1788 Le Vade at Robinson's. Jean David Paul Etienne LeVade (A de
                            Montet, Dictionnaire Biographique des Genevois et des Vaudois) born
                            Lausanne 2.10.1750 died there 9.1.1834 was a minister in England then
                            Amsterdam. His translation of Tristram Shandy into French was published
                            1786 in York and Paris, and a translation of his True and Surprising
                            Account of a Natural Sleepwalker, given as a lecture in Lausanne
                            6.2.1788, was published in Edinburgh in 1792</p>
